(Page 6 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(6) Tj T*
(Introduction: Models, Tools and Agents) Tj T*
(Without access to external functions, even the most advanced foundation model1 is just) Tj T*
(a pattern prediction engine. An advanced model can do many things well -- passing law) Tj T*
(exams2, writing code3 or poetry4, creating images5 and videos6, solving math problems7) Tj T*
(-- but on its own it can only generate content based on the data it was previously trained) Tj T*
(on. It can't access any new data about the world except what is fed into it in its request) Tj T*
(context; it can't interact with an external system; and it can't take any action to influence) Tj T*
(its environment.) Tj T*
(Most modern foundation models now have the capacity to call external functions, or tools,) Tj T*
(to address this limitation. Like apps on a smartphone, tools enable an AI system to do more) Tj T*
(than just generate patterns. These tools act as the agent's "eyes" and "hands," allowing it to) Tj T*
(perceive and act on the world.) Tj T*
(Unifying Agents, Tools, and) Tj T*
(the World) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
