(Page 7 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(7) Tj T*
(With the advent of Agentic AI, tools become even more important to AI systems. An AI Agent) Tj T*
(uses a foundation model's reasoning capability to interact with users and achieve specific) Tj T*
(goals for them, and external tools give the agent that capacity. With the capacity to take) Tj T*
(external actions, agents can have a dramatic impact on enterprise applications.8) Tj T*
(Connecting external tools to foundation models carries significant challenges, though, both) Tj T*
(basic technical issues as well as important security risks. The Model Context Protocol9 was) Tj T*
(introduced in 2024 as a way to streamline the process of integrating tools and models, and) Tj T*
(address some of these technical and security challenges.) Tj T*
(In this paper we talk first about the nature of tools used by foundation models: what they are) Tj T*
(and how to use them. We give some best practices and guidelines for designing effective) Tj T*
(tools and using them effectively. We then look at the Model Context Protocol, talking about) Tj T*
(its basic components and some of the challenges and risks it entails. Finally, we take a) Tj T*
(deeper look at the security challenges posed by MCP as it is introduced in an enterprise) Tj T*
(environment and connected to high-value external systems.) Tj T*
(To facilitate this transition from AI experimentation to secure, production-scale agentic) Tj T*
(systems, Google Cloud has evolved Vertex AI into the Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform. This) Tj T*
(comprehensive, end-to-end platform is designed around four foundational pillars: Build,) Tj T*
(Scale, Govern, and Optimize. By providing native infrastructure for tool integration, state) Tj T*
(management, and strict enterprise security, the platform allows organizations to deploy) Tj T*
(robust autonomous agents with confidence.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
