(Page 8 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(8) Tj T*
(Tools and tool calling) Tj T*
(What do we mean by a tool?) Tj T*
(In the world of modern AI, a tool is a function or a program an LLM-based application) Tj T*
(can use to accomplish a task outside the model's capabilities. The model itself generates) Tj T*
(content to respond to the user's question; tools let the application interact with other) Tj T*
(systems. Broadly speaking, tools fit into 2 types: they allow a model to know something or) Tj T*
(to do something. In other words, tools can retrieve data for the model to use in subsequent) Tj T*
(requests, by accessing structured and unstructured data sources; or, tools can perform an) Tj T*
(action on behalf of the user, often by calling an external API or by executing some other code) Tj T*
(or function.) Tj T*
(An example application of a tool for an agent might include calling an API to get the weather) Tj T*
(forecast for the user's location, and presenting the information in the user's preferred units.) Tj T*
(This is a simple question, but to answer this correctly the model would need information) Tj T*
(about the user's current location and the current weather -- neither of those data points are) Tj T*
(included in the model's training data. The model also needs to be able to convert between) Tj T*
(temperature units; while foundation models are improving in their mathematical capabilities,) Tj T*
(this is not their strong suit and math computations are another area where it is generally best) Tj T*
(to call on an external function.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
