(Page 10 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(10) Tj T*
(Function Tools) Tj T*
(All models that support function calling10 allow the developer to define external functions) Tj T*
(that the model can call as needed. The tool's definition should provide basic details about) Tj T*
(how the model should use the tool; this is provided to the model as part of the request) Tj T*
(context. In a Python framework like Google ADK, the definition passed to the model is) Tj T*
(extracted from the Python docstring in the tool code as in the example below.) Tj T*
(This example shows a tool defined for Google ADK11 that calls an external function to change) Tj T*
(the brightness of a light. The set_light_values is passed a ToolContext object \(part of) Tj T*
(the Google ADK framework\) to provide more details about the request context.) Tj T*
(Snippet 1: Definition for set_light_values tool) Tj T*
(Python) Tj T*
(def set_light_values\() Tj T*
(brightness: int,) Tj T*
(color_temp: str,) Tj T*
(context: ToolContext\) -> dict[str, int | str]:) Tj T*
("""This tool sets the brightness and color temperature of the room lights) Tj T*
(in the user's current location.) Tj T*
(Args:) Tj T*
(brightness: Light level from 0 to 100. Zero is off and 100 is full) Tj T*
(brightness) Tj T*
(color_temp: Color temperature of the light fixture, which can be) Tj T*
(`daylight`, `cool` or `warm`.) Tj T*
(context: A ToolContext object used to retrieve the user's location.) Tj T*
(Returns:) Tj T*
(A dictionary containing the set brightness and color temperature.) Tj T*
(""") Tj T*
(user_room_id = context.state['room_id']) Tj T*
(# This is an imaginary room lighting control API) Tj T*
(room = light_system.get_room\(user_room_id\)) Tj T*
(response = room.set_lights\(brightness, color_temp\)) Tj T*
(return {"tool_response": response}) Tj T*
ET
endstream
