(Page 11 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(11) Tj T*
(Built-in tools) Tj T*
(Some foundation models offer the ability to leverage built in tools, where the tool definition) Tj T*
(is given to the model implicitly, or behind the scenes of the model service. Google's Gemini) Tj T*
(API, for instance, provides several built-in tools: Grounding with Google Search12, Code) Tj T*
(Execution13, URL Context14, and Computer Use15.) Tj T*
(This example below shows how to invoke the Gemini built-in url_context tool. The tool) Tj T*
(definition itself is invisible to the developer; it's provided to the model separately.) Tj T*
(Python) Tj T*
(from google import genai) Tj T*
(from google.genai.types import \() Tj T*
(Tool,) Tj T*
(GenerateContentConfig,) Tj T*
(HttpOptions,) Tj T*
(UrlContext) Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
(client = genai.Client\(http_options=HttpOptions\(api_version="v1"\)) Tj T*
(model_id = "gemini-2.5-flash") Tj T*
(url_context_tool = Tool\() Tj T*
(url_context = UrlContext) Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
(url1 =) Tj T*
("https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/ina-garten/perfect-roast-chicken-recipe-19) Tj T*
(40592") Tj T*
(url2 = "https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/70679/simple-whole-roasted-chicken/") Tj T*
(Continues next page...) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
