(Page 12 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(12) Tj T*
(Snippet 2: Calling url_context tool) Tj T*
(Agent Tools) Tj T*
(An agent can also be invoked as a tool. This prevents a full handoff of the user conversation,) Tj T*
(allowing the primary agent to maintain control over the interaction and process the sub-) Tj T*
(agent's input and output as needed. In ADK, this is accomplished by using the AgentTool16) Tj T*
(class in the SDK. Google's A2A protocol17, discussed in Day 5: Prototype to Production,) Tj T*
(even allows you to make remote agents available as tools. In ADK, this is accomplished by) Tj T*
(using the AgentTool class in the SDK. Recently, the ADK has received a major upgrade with) Tj T*
(version 2.x, introducing a powerful graph-based framework that enables developers to) Tj T*
(organize individual agents into a sophisticated network of sub-agents.) Tj T*
(response = client.models.generate_content\() Tj T*
(model=model_id,) Tj T*
(contents=\("Compare the ingredients and cooking times from ") Tj T*
(f"the recipes at {url1} and {url2}"\),) Tj T*
(config=GenerateContentConfig\() Tj T*
(tools=[url_context_tool],) Tj T*
(response_modalities=["TEXT"],) Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
(for each in response.candidates[0].content.parts:) Tj T*
(print\(each.text\)) Tj T*
(# For verification, you can inspect the metadata to see which URLs the) Tj T*
(model retrieved) Tj T*
(print\(response.candidates[0].url_context_metadata\)) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
