(Page 15 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(15) Tj T*
(Documentation is important) Tj T*
(The tool documentation \(name, description and attributes\) are all passed to the model as) Tj T*
(a part of the request context, so all of these are important to help the model use the tool) Tj T*
(correctly.) Tj T*
(* Use a clear name: The name of the tool should be clearly descriptive, human readable,) Tj T*
(and specific to help the model decide which tool to use. For instance, create_) Tj T*
(critical_bug_in_jira_with_priority is clearer than update_jira. This is also) Tj T*
(important for governance; if tool calls are logged, having clear names will make audit logs) Tj T*
(more informative.) Tj T*
(* Describe all input and output parameters: All inputs to the tool should be clearly) Tj T*
(described, including both the required type and the use the tool will make of) Tj T*
(the parameter.) Tj T*
(* Simplify parameter lists: Long parameter lists can confuse the model; keep them) Tj T*
(parameter lists short and give parameters clear names.) Tj T*
(* Clarify tool descriptions: Provide a clear, detailed description of the input and output) Tj T*
(parameters, the purpose of the tool, and any other details needed to call the tool) Tj T*
(effectively. Avoid shorthand or technical jargon; focus on clear explanations using) Tj T*
(simple terminology.) Tj T*
(* Add targeted examples: Examples can help address ambiguities, show how to handle) Tj T*
(tricky requests, or clarify distinctions in terminology. They can also be a way to refine and) Tj T*
(target model behavior without resorting to more expensive approaches like fine tuning.) Tj T*
(You can also dynamically retrieve examples related to the immediate task to minimize) Tj T*
(context bloat.) Tj T*
(* Provide default values: Provide default values for key parameters and be sure to) Tj T*
(document and describe the default values in the tool documentation. LLMs can often use) Tj T*
(default values correctly, if they are well-documented.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
