(The following are examples of good and bad tool documentation.) Tj T*
(Snippet 4: Good tool documentation) Tj T*
(Python) Tj T*
(def get_product_information\(product_id: str\) -> dict:) Tj T*
(""") Tj T*
(Retrieves comprehensive information about a product based on the unique) Tj T*
(product ID.) Tj T*
(Args:) Tj T*
(product_id: The unique identifier for the product.) Tj T*
(Returns:) Tj T*
(A dictionary containing product details. Expected keys include:) Tj T*
('product_name': The name of the product.) Tj T*
('brand': The brand name of the product) Tj T*
('description': A paragraph of text describing the product.) Tj T*
('category': The category of the product.) Tj T*
('status': The current status of the product \(e.g., 'active',) Tj T*
('inactive', 'suspended'\).) Tj T*
(Example return value:) Tj T*
({) Tj T*
('product_name': 'Astro Zoom Kid's Trainers',) Tj T*
('brand': 'Cymbal Athletic Shoes',) Tj T*
('description': '...',) Tj T*
('category': 'Children's Shoes',) Tj T*
('status': 'active') Tj T*
(}) Tj T*
(""") Tj T*
ET
