(Page 18 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(18) Tj T*
(Publish tasks, not API calls) Tj T*
(Tools should encapsulate a task the agent needs to perform, not an external API. It's easy) Tj T*
(to write tools that are just thin wrappers over the existing API surface, but this is a mistake.) Tj T*
(Instead, tool developers should define tools that clearly capture specific actions the agent) Tj T*
(might take on behalf of the user, and document the specific action and the parameters) Tj T*
(needed. APIs are intended to be used by human developers with full knowledge of the) Tj T*
(available data and the API parameters; complex Enterprise APIs can have tens or even) Tj T*
(hundreds of possible parameters that influence the API output. Tools for agents, by contrast,) Tj T*
(are expected to be used dynamically, by an agent that needs to decide at runtime which) Tj T*
(parameters to use and what data to pass. If the tool represents a specific task the agent) Tj T*
(should accomplish, the agent is much more likely to be able to call it correctly.) Tj T*
(Make tools as granular as possible) Tj T*
(Keeping functions concise and limited to a single function is standard coding best practice;) Tj T*
(follow this guidance when defining tools too. This makes it easier to document the tool and) Tj T*
(allows the agent to be more consistent in determining when the tool is needed.) Tj T*
(* Define clear responsibilities: Make sure each tool has a clear, well-documented) Tj T*
(purpose. What does it do? When should it be called? Does it have any side effects? What) Tj T*
(data will it return?) Tj T*
(* Don't create multi-tools: In general, don't create tools that take many steps in turn or) Tj T*
(encapsulate a long workflow. These can be complicated to document and maintain, and) Tj T*
(can be difficult for LLMs to use consistently. There are scenarios when such a tool may) Tj T*
(be useful -- for instance, if a commonly performed workflow requires many tool calls in) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
