(Page 21 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(21) Tj T*
(Anthropic introduced the Model Context Protocol \(MCP\) in November 2024 as an open) Tj T*
(standard to begin addressing this situation. The goal of MCP from the outset has been to) Tj T*
(replace the fragmented landscape of custom integrations with a unified, plug-and-play) Tj T*
(protocol that could serve as a universal interface between AI applications and the vast world) Tj T*
(of external tools and data. By standardizing this communication layer, MCP aims to decouple) Tj T*
(the AI agent from the specific implementation details of the tools it uses, allowing for a more) Tj T*
(modular, scalable, and efficient ecosystem.) Tj T*
(Core Architectural Components: Hosts, Clients, and Servers) Tj T*
(The Model Context Protocol implements a client-server model, inspired by the Language) Tj T*
(Server Protocol \(LSP\) in the software development world.9 This architecture separates the AI) Tj T*
(application from the tool integrations and allows a more modular and extensible approach to) Tj T*
(tool development. The core MCP components are the Host, the Client, and the Server.) Tj T*
(* MCP Host: The application responsible for creating and managing individual MCP clients;) Tj T*
(may be a standalone application, or a sub-component of a larger system such as a multi-) Tj T*
(agent system. Responsibilities include managing the user experience, orchestrating the) Tj T*
(use of tools, and enforcing security policies and content guardrails.) Tj T*
(* MCP Client: A software component embedded within the Host that maintains the) Tj T*
(connection with the Server. The responsibilities of the client are issuing commands,) Tj T*
(receiving responses, and managing the lifecycle of the communication session with its) Tj T*
(MCP Server.) Tj T*
(* MCP Server: A program that provides a set of capabilities the server developer wants) Tj T*
(to make available to AI applications, often functioning as an adapter or a proxy for an) Tj T*
(external tool, data source, or API. Primary responsibilities are advertising available tools) Tj T*
(\(tool discovery\), receiving and executing commands, and formatting and returning) Tj T*
(results. In enterprise contexts, servers are also responsible for security, scalability) Tj T*
(and governance.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
