(Page 33 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(33) Tj T*
(Sampling) Tj T*
(Sampling26 is a client-side capability that allows an MCP server to request an LLM completion) Tj T*
(from the client. If one of the server's capabilities needs input from an LLM, instead of) Tj T*
(implementing the LLM call and using the results internally, the server would issue a Sampling) Tj T*
(request back to the client for the client to execute. This reverses the typical flow of control,) Tj T*
(allowing a tool to leverage the Host's core AI model to perform a sub-task, such as asking) Tj T*
(the LLM to summarize a large document the server just fetched. The MCP specification) Tj T*
(recommends that clients insert a human in the loop stage in Sampling, so that there is always) Tj T*
(the option for a user to deny a server's Sampling request.) Tj T*
(Sampling presents both opportunities and challenges for developers. By offloading LLM) Tj T*
(calls to the client, Sampling gives client developers control over the LLM providers used in) Tj T*
(their applications, and allows costs to be borne by the application developer instead of the) Tj T*
(service provider. Sampling also gives the client developer control of any content guardrails) Tj T*
(and security filters required around the LLM call, and provides a clean way to insert a) Tj T*
(human approval step for LLM requests that occur in the application's execution path. On the) Tj T*
(other hand, like the Prompt capability, Sampling also opens an avenue for potential prompt) Tj T*
(injection in the client application. Clients should take care to filter and validate any prompt) Tj T*
(accompanying a sampling request, and should ensure that the human-in-the-loop control) Tj T*
(phase is implemented with effective controls for users to interact with the sampling request.) Tj T*
(Elicitation) Tj T*
(Elicitation27 is another client-side capability, similar to Sampling, that allows an MCP server) Tj T*
(to request additional user information from the client. Instead of requesting an LLM call, an) Tj T*
(MCP tool using Elicitation can query the host application dynamically for additional data to) Tj T*
(complete the tool request. Elicitation provides a formal mechanism for a server to pause) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
