stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
36 756 Td
13 TL
(Page 46 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(46) Tj T*
(Malicious Tool Definitions and Consumed Contents) Tj T*
(Risk) Tj T*
(Tool descriptor fields, including their documentation and API signature35, can manipulate) Tj T*
(agent planners into executing rogue actions. Tools might ingest external content36) Tj T*
(containing injectable prompts, leading to agent manipulation even if the tool's own definition) Tj T*
(is benign. Tool return values can also lead to data exfiltration issues; for instance, a tool) Tj T*
(query may return personal data about a user or confidential information about the company,) Tj T*
(which the agent may pass on unfiltered to the user.) Tj T*
(Mitigations) Tj T*
(* Input Validation: Sanitize and validate all user inputs to prevent the execution of malicious) Tj T*
(/ abusive commands or code. For instance, if an AI is asked to "list files in the reports) Tj T*
(directory," the filter should prevent it from accessing a different, sensitive directory like) Tj T*
(../../secrets. Products such as GCP's Model Armor37 can help with sanitizing prompts.) Tj T*
(* Output Sanitization: Sanitize any data returned from tools before feeding it back into the) Tj T*
(model's context to remove potential malicious content. Some examples of data that should) Tj T*
(be caught by an output filter are API tokens, social security and credit card numbers,) Tj T*
(active content such as Markdown and HTML, or certain data types including URLs or) Tj T*
(email addresses.) Tj T*
(* Separate System Prompts: Clearly separate user inputs from system instructions to) Tj T*
(prevent a user from tampering with core model behavior. Taking this a step further, one) Tj T*
(could build an agent with two separate planners, a trusted planner with access to first-) Tj T*
(party or authenticated MCP tools, and an untrusted planner with access to third-party) Tj T*
(MCP tools, with only a restricted communication channel between them.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
97 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 98 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> >>
endobj
98 0 obj
<< /Length 1942 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
36 756 Td
13 TL
(Page 47 of 56 - 03 - Agent Tools &  Interoperability  with MCP) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability with MCP) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(47) Tj T*
(* Strict allowlist validation and sanitization of MCP resources: Consumption of) Tj T*
(resources \(e.g., data files, images\) from 3P servers must be via URLs that are validated) Tj T*
(against an allowlist. MCP clients should implement a user consent model that requires) Tj T*
(users to explicitly select resources before they can be used.) Tj T*
(* Sanitize Tool Descriptions as part of policy enforcement through an AI Gateway or policy) Tj T*
(engine before they are injected into the LLM's context.) Tj T*
(Sensitive information Leaks) Tj T*
(Risk) Tj T*
(In the course of a user interaction, MCP tools may unintentionally \(or in the case of malicious) Tj T*
(tools, intentionally\) receive sensitive information, leading to data exfiltration. The contents of) Tj T*
(a user interaction are frequently stored in the conversation context and transmitted to agent) Tj T*
(tools, which may not be authorized to access this data.) Tj T*
(The new Elicitation server capability adds to this risk. Although, as discussed above, the) Tj T*
(MCP spec explicitly specifies38 that Elicitation should not require sensitive information from) Tj T*
(the client, there is no enforcement of this policy, and a malicious Server may easily violate) Tj T*
(this recommendation.) Tj T*
(Mitigations) Tj T*
(* MCP tools should use structured outputs and use annotations on input/output) Tj T*
(fields: Tool outputs carrying sensitive information should be clearly identified with a) Tj T*
(tag or annotation so they can be identified as sensitive by the client. To do this, custom) Tj T*
(annotations can be  implemented to identify, track, and control the flow of sensitive data.) Tj T*
(Frameworks must be able to analyze the outputs and verify their format.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
99 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 100 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> >>
